  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: cbb4df94e5a55d64ab78b56ec3baa0b5, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q8
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::HistoricalQuestionData
  questionID: Q8
  questionText: Which king returned the magic sword to the Golden Turtle at Ta Vong
    Lake (Ho Guom Lake)?
  answers:
  - Le Loi
  - Nguyen Hue
  - Tran Nhan Tong
  - Ly Cong Uan
  correctAnswerIndex: 0
  answerFeedbacks:
  - Exactly! After driving out the Ming army, King Le Thai To (Le Loi) returned the
    Thuan Thien sword to the Golden Turtle, and from then on the lake was named Hoan
    Kiem Lake.
  - Wrong! King Quang Trung (Nguyen Hue) was a hero who, wearing simple clothes and
    carrying a red banner, decisively defeated 290,000 Qing troops.
  - Wrong! Tran Nhan Tong was a wise king of the Tran dynasty, the founder of the
    Truc Lam Yen Tu Zen sect.
  - Wrong! Ly Cong Uan (Ly Thai To) was the person who issued the decree to move
    the capital from Hoa Lu to Thang Long in 1010.
  difficultyTier: 1
